{#
    One button, and the element draws all of it.

    **Every option is a property** — the variant, the size, the state, where it
    goes. Nothing here says what a button looks like: not the shape, not the
    height, not what the label is wrapped in. That is what the component is for.

    Two things are not attributes. The label is written between the tags,
    because that is where `sds-button` takes it and because a glyph beside the
    words is a node — which is the other one: `:icon:` becomes `sds-icon`
    composed into the control, exactly as a page of this system writes it.

    The label is the argument's words and not its markup. A reference rendered
    in place would put an `<a>` inside the control; the reference is where the
    press goes instead, and it lands on the element as `href`. `:href:` is the
    same thing said as a path, and wins where both are written.
#}
{%- set href = node.option('href') ? renderLink(node.option('href')) : linkUrl(node.link) -%}
{%- set label = node.title.toString -%}
{%- set glyph = node.option('icon') -%}
{#- A control whose whole label is a glyph is named by nothing else, so the
    words that would have been the label become the title. The element cannot
    work the shape out for itself here: it is handed markup rather than nodes
    when a page is rendered ahead of the browser, and a square button that lost
    its shape is a round control gone rectangular in a row. -#}
{%- set only = glyph and node.option('icon-only') -%}
{%- set title = node.option('title') ?: (only ? label : '') -%}
<sds-button
    {%- if href %} href="{{ href }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if node.option('variant') %} variant="{{ node.option('variant') }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if node.option('size') %} size="{{ node.option('size') }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if only %} icon-only{% endif %}
    {%- if title %} title="{{ title }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if node.option('rel') %} rel="{{ node.option('rel') }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if node.option('disabled') %} disabled{% endif %}
    {%- if node.option('class') %} class="{{ node.option('class') }}"{% endif %}
>{% if glyph %}<sds-icon name="{{ glyph }}"></sds-icon>{% endif %}{% if not only %}{{ label }}{% endif %}</sds-button>
